#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:2 a7a58590ad9d4c56b1ce218cc9e2e530
msgid "When something is wrong"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:4 aa58a5fdc17d44d38d5966b243b06eea
msgid "The usual causes, what each looks like, and the command that settles it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:11
#: f3731bdc744547fd8aa37143cd3a2078
msgid "Three answers that disagree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:13
#: 0cb134d6117642eb9ec0c430b0643573
msgid ""
"A drive's state can be asked three ways, and they do not always agree. "
"This is the single most confusing thing about MHVTL, and it is worth "
"knowing before it happens:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:28
#: e5494074a12647f8a091743c13967de9
msgid ""
"That was a real drive with a real cartridge in it, which wrote and read "
"back perfectly. ``mt`` was simply stale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:31
#: 43fa0b4db8034b92b87836cafae2c572
msgid ""
"**Believe the robot.** The robot moved the cartridge and knows where it "
"is, and it keeps answering during a backup. So does the drive's own "
"counter page. ``mt`` is the one that stops: the program writing has the "
"tape device open, and the kernel gives that to one writer at a time, so "
"``mt`` says *device busy* until the backup finishes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:38
#: 2ce1a1e3e39240d5be3d74c1ca1f0de5
msgid "\"Restart the library for its robot to see this\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:40
#: 7e43c2c47f374a3faa9ab3bf33761bb5
msgid ""
"MHVTL reads its configuration **once**, when a daemon starts. Adding a "
"tape, adopting one, or changing the slot count edits the file, and the "
"running robot knows nothing about it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:50
#: 41afc146971f4a059f932731a82e151b
msgid ""
"Until you do, ``mhvtl tape list`` shows the new cartridge and ``mhvtl "
"status library`` does not. The console says the same on the library page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:58
#: 91c24a6644c64a1884bae7ddd8504584
msgid "A drive says ``silent``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:60
#: 541bf579e9a54ccbb34c7bfb2afa9ecb
msgid ""
"Its daemon is not running. Nothing is broken about the library; that one "
"drive is simply absent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:76
#: 76986592917a4a0f9288c554aae77f34
msgid "A library page that answers 404"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:78
#: 031c532c25f94c938ee3eff61c0774f6
msgid ""
"A library made from the command line exists in the configuration before "
"the console's database hears of it. Opening the page syncs it first, so "
"this should be rare. If it persists:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:88
#: 021ad6d2f5a74b9994e0ca2b1cf493c7
msgid "An export that points at the wrong device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:90
#: 73f974b9b76e4d058d7d5a6e73e65bc9
msgid ""
"``/dev/sg`` numbers change when the MHVTL module reloads and when a "
"library is recreated. An iSCSI export remembers a node, so after either "
"it may be pointing at something else entirely:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:102
#: 6e17be59afb243a5943a8dddc32fc69d
msgid ""
"This runs at boot as well. The iSCSI page shows the same per device: "
"**Created on**, **Device now**, and whether they agree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:106
#: 030cbd2f0ab3432c8171c5533b7a2f6d
msgid "Tapes that belong to no library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:108
#: 75112635a8a44d3eabf6ecbc541b751c
msgid ""
"Removing a library leaves its cartridges on disk on purpose - they are "
"data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:121
#: 886ebd46e27e4dcd8cd3cbea53cbab44
msgid "See :doc:`../tapes/adopt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:124
#: b111e014dae1435ea320a70028aa9ed6
msgid "A drive that will not take a cartridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:126
#: d0d60584515c4959a50cd3baed263d11
msgid "Check that the drive writes that generation at all:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:132
#: f1bf69d18eea4806a8a35171a194fe6b
msgid ""
"A drive reads older cartridges and writes recent ones, as the real "
"hardware does. Mounting an LTO-5 cartridge into an LTO-8 drive is allowed"
" and reading it works; writing to it does not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:137
#: e8db3ef131364acea9785bc757dead72
msgid "The disk is full"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:139
#: 95ecd23ec92444609ff6e8fff3c5d795
msgid ""
"Tapes are files, so a full disk fails writes in ways that look like drive"
" faults:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:146
#: 70aeef2fb54840bd825fa07564defda2
msgid ""
"A cartridge occupies only what has been written to it, so the problem is "
"usually one library that has had a great deal written to it, not the "
"number of cartridges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:151
#: dc1908aba898411da6c43634bd61eb8b
msgid "Removing a library and rebooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:153
#: 837b6be0184e4096bd034f8b1cb26b13
msgid ""
"On this host the kernel ``ch`` driver is blacklisted, because it takes a "
"reference on every drive a changer reports and never releases it - the "
"drives' SCSI addresses then stay unusable until a reboot. If a newly "
"created library is missing drives, or ``rmmod mhvtl`` says the module is "
"in use with everything stopped, read *The kernel ch driver leak* in the "
"*Guides*. Only a reboot clears it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:161
#: f9efebe5eb5a44a0a31a4058fbf08ede
msgid "Which version am I running"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:163
#: 089e40d32e2343e192ca9efb8c6b0292
msgid ""
"Worth settling first, because a problem that was fixed in a later release"
" looks exactly like a problem. Three places answer it, and all three read"
" the same value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:176
#: 2b80b05db5634cefb8ddd904404ba3d4
msgid ""
"``mhvtl status system`` prints it above the rest of the host's state, "
"which makes it the one command to quote in a bug report:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:192
#: 5706c57652a14f71854687b761df4af8
msgid ""
"In the console it is **About**, in the header of every page. That page "
"adds what the command line cannot easily show - the Python and Django "
"versions, the kernel, and the host's name - which is the rest of what a "
"bug report needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:199
#: a0999bcc16624e23ab2192a188a41ce7
msgid ""
"**The program is** ``mhvtl-console``; **the package is** ``mhvtl-gui``. "
"Both names are correct and they mean different things. ``mhvtl-console`` "
"is the product, which is what the version line and the About page say. "
"``mhvtl-gui`` is the RPM, the directory ``/opt/mhvtl-gui``, the account "
"the service runs as, and the unit ``mhvtl-gui.service`` - so ``rpm -q``, "
"``systemctl`` and the paths all keep the older name. It was renamed in "
"3.3.0 because an unrelated, older interface to MHVTL is also called "
"mhvtl-gui, and a bug report quoting a version could not say which program"
" it was about."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:209
#: 3aa5144f738c46d88838d0037c57d279
msgid ""
"The last line, ``running from``, is which copy of the code answered. A "
"host can carry two - the installed tree under ``/opt/mhvtl-gui`` and a "
"developer's checkout - and they print the same version, so one typed "
"command can be two different programs. ``sudo`` always resolves "
"``/usr/bin/mhvtl`` and therefore the installed tree, because sudoers sets"
" ``secure_path``; plain ``mhvtl`` can be pointed elsewhere by ``PATH``. "
"If a command behaves unlike the documentation, read this line first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:217
#: 4c97c26aec0d466986402ba7b49f16a1
msgid ""
"If the page and the command disagree, the service was upgraded and not "
"restarted: the workers hold the code they started with. ``systemctl "
"restart mhvtl-gui`` settles it. The packaged RPM restarts the service on "
"an upgrade for exactly this reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:223
#: 22a9ba2afbed4557917fff57779d1fb3
msgid "Nothing here helped"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:225
#: bfc7ddd5d0004bfb8cb5b0036d96f8b5
msgid "The logs say what the drive was actually asked to do:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/when-something-is-wrong.rst:231
#: 60001e83744043e6a8a2599979c6da32
msgid "and the configuration can be checked against itself:"
msgstr ""

